rn Seremban.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sungbos-eredo"><span class="enc-name">Sungbo's Eredo</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Sungbo's Eredo is a system of earthworks, a ditch and bank about 160 kilometres long, surrounding the area of Ijebu-Ode in south-western Nigeria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sunifred-of-urgell"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sunifred-of-urgell.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sunifred of Urgell</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sunifred was a 9th-century Frankish count who ruled Urgell and Cerdanya from about 834 and also Barcelona, Girona and other counties of the Spanish March from 844 until…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/suniti-devi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/suniti-devi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Suniti Devi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Suniti Devi was Maharani of Cooch Behar, the daughter of the reformer Keshab Chandra Sen and wife of Maharaja Nripendra Narayan, whom she married in 1878.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sunjong-of-korea"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sunjong-of-korea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sunjong of Korea</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sunjong of Korea was the second and last emperor of the Korean Empire, reigning from 1907 to 1910 under the era name Yunghui.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sunni-ali"><span class="enc-name">Sunni Ali</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sunni Ali was ruler of Songhai from 1464 to 1492 and the founder of the Songhai Empire.</span></a></li><li