</span><span class="enc-snip">The Supermarine Spitfire was a British single-seat fighter aircraft designed by R.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/suphanburi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/suphanburi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Suphanburi</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Suphanburi is a city in central Thailand on the Tha Chin river, north-west of Bangkok.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/suppiluliuma-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/suppiluliuma-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Suppiluliuma I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Suppiluliuma I was a king of the Hittite Empire who reigned c. 1344–1322 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/suppiluliuma-ii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/suppiluliuma-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Suppiluliuma II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Suppiluliuma II was the last known king of the Hittite Empire, reigning from about 1207 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/supplementary-fundamental-law"><span class="enc-name">Supplementary Fundamental Law</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Supplementary Fundamental Law was the second part of the Persian Constitution, ratified in October 1907 by Mohammad Ali Shah.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/supreme-commander-for-the-allied-powers"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/supreme-commander-for-the-allied-powers.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Supreme Commander for the Allied Powers</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="e